# Frontend configuration. All three are REQUIRED -- there is deliberately no
# fallback in the source any more. A missing or misspelled value must fail
# loudly rather than silently pointing a dev or staging bundle at the production
# project, which is exactly what the old defaults did. It fails when the page
# loads in the browser (blank app, error in the console); `npm run build` still
# succeeds without these, so a green build does not prove they are set.
#
# The anon key is safe to expose in a public build: it only satisfies the Edge
# Functions gateway's own JWT check. The real privilege boundary is
# requireUser() and the role checks inside each function
# (supabase/functions/_shared/auth.ts).

# Local development against `supabase start` (the values below are the
# standard local demo credentials, not secrets):
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<run `supabase status` and copy the anon key>

# For a deployed build, set these in the Vercel project settings instead:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   VITE_FUNCTIONS_BASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<the project's anon/publishable key>
